# Simple YouTube Pomodoro - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
- React (Vite) + Tailwind CSS
- YouTube IFrame Player API (react-youtube)
- LocalStorage for data persistence
- No backend, no user authentication (MVP)

## Coding Standards
- Use functional components with Hooks
- Follow PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling (inline classes)
- Keep functions small and focused (single responsibility)
- Add comments for complex logic

## File Structure
- Components: src/components/
- Custom Hooks: src/hooks/
- Utilities: src/utils/
- Custom Hooks: src/hooks/
- Utilities: src/utils/

## Implementation Priority
1. Timer countdown (useState, useEffect)
2. YouTube player integration (react-youtube)
3. LocalStorage persistence (custom hook)
4. URL input form & playlist management
5. Auto-play next track

## Best Practices
- Avoid magic numbers (use constants)
- Use useMemo/useCallback to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Handle errors gracefully (alert for user input, console.error for API errors)
- Keep YouTube player visible (minimum 200x200px, API requirement)

